+++ b/docs/goldens/SCHEMA.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Golden schema — `docs/goldens/probe-seed42-ticks100.json` (single source)
+
+*Slice 1 (story 1.1): the golden JSON schema is single-sourced HERE. The
+three writers — `tests/spine_check.cpp` (`--json` printf), the `PPProbe`
+commandlet (`PPProbeCommandlet.cpp`), and `scripts/compare-golden.sh`
+(KEYS) — all derive from this document; a key added/renamed here must be
+mirrored in all three, and the golden + the inline spine-check CHECKs
+re-blessed together (deliberate + cause-documented, AGENTS.md golden
+discipline).*
+
+## The run the golden pins
+
+`seed=42`, `ticks=100`, the full slice-1 scenario (`PP_Scenario.h` —
+shared by every surface so the numbers CANNOT drift, UAD-17):
+
+- fixture: source terminal (2,2), router junction (6,2), sink terminal
+  (10,2) — spawned as run setup (NOT in the action log)
+- draw commands: source→router + router→sink (standard tier), logged with
+  `apply_tick=1`, applied by the replay path at tick 1
+- demand: class-0 packets source→sink every 10 ticks (5..95) + one at 98
+  (in-flight at the boundary) — run setup, NOT in the action log
+
+Delivered = 10, in-flight at tick 100 = 1 (at the router), score = 10.
+The heartbeat (`tick_nonce`) is UNCHANGED from the v1 golden — the scenario
+draws no rng (legacy demand + pure-hash ECMP), so the RNG contract held
+byte-exact through the re-bless.
+
+## Schema (keys in canonical order)
+
+| Key | Type | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `seed` | u64 | the run seed (42) |
+| `ticks` | int | the step count (100) |
+| `tick_nonce` | u32 | the heartbeat draw after the last step (one owned-RNG draw per step, ODN-9) |
+| `state_hash` | hex-string u64 | FNV-1a-64 over the canonical serialized state (`PP::StateHash`), v2 layout |
+| `rng_first4` | [u32 ×4] | the first 4 draws of a FRESH seed-42 stream (drawn before the run; pins the ODN-9 vector independent of the run's heartbeat) |
+| `save_magic` | "PPUE" | the LE wire magic (ODN-11) |
+| `save_version` | int | the serialized layout version (2 — slice-1 v2 layout: catalog_hash/score/replay_error/topology/flow/action-log sections added; deliberate re-bless, SCHEMA + spine-check + golden updated together) |
+| `catalog_hash` | hex-string u64 | FNV-1a-64 over the loaded catalogs' canonical concatenation. Slice 1 loads NO catalogs → the empty-set hash (`FNV64_OFFSET` = `cbf29ce484222325`), pinned; drift becomes a defined rejection when the first catalog lands (3.1, UAD-5) |
+| `topology_summary.nodes` | int | live node count |
+| `topology_summary.pipes` | int | live pipe count |
+| `topology_summary.gen` | u32 | the Topology.Gen after the run (every spawn/draw bumps it — the rule-1 rebuild trigger) |
+| `forwarding_summary.reachable_pairs` | int | (from,dst) slots with ≥1 equal-cost next hop in the final routing table |
+| `forwarding_summary.total_hops` | int | Σ hop counts over the table (ECMP set sizes) |
+| `flow_summary.spawned` | int | packets constructed = delivered + live (the SAME formula on both golden writers — the r2 warning: PPProbe used Demand.size(), which counts demand ENTRIES; unified to delivered + live) |
+| `flow_summary.delivered` | int | packets delivered at the sink |
+| `flow_summary.live` | int | in-flight packets at the final tick |
+| `flow_summary.score` | int | the run score (delivered count — the 1.4 win metric) |
+
+## v1 → v2 re-bless record (the cause, per AGENTS.md discipline)
+
+- **When:** slice 1, story 1.1 (the sim spine grows into the engine).
+- **What changed:** the serialized state layout grew (v1 = seed/tick/nonce/
+  rng/terminal only → v2 = + catalog_hash, score, replay_error, topology
+  (nodes+pipes+gen), flow (packets+demand+next_packet_id), action log) and
+  the golden run now exercises the FULL slice-1 scenario (fixture + draws +
+  demand) instead of an empty run.
+- **Proof the fold is honest:** `tick_nonce` (2381141952) and `rng_first4`
+  are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the v1 golden — the RNG contract did not move; only
+  the extended state changed the hash. `state_hash` fbe6fae2655cadf7 →
+  **5e440f9c5a28892a**.
+- **Both surfaces updated together:** this golden + the inline CHECKs in
+  `tests/spine_check.cpp` (+ the mirrored `PacketPlumber.*` automation
+  asserts and the engine probe, which derives from the same scenario).
