+# Look-parity checklist — slice-1 baseline (UAD-22)
+
+*2026-08-21 · story 1.2/1.3 evidence surface. The MM reference frame stays
+LOCAL (IP guardrail — never committed); the committed surface is the UE
+frame + THIS score.*
+
+The slice-1 look-parity target (user ruling 2026-08-20 evening): the static
+fixture renders in the Mini Motorways look and is scored against the actual
+MM frame across the five checklist axes. Scores: ✅ = matches the MM look,
+🟡 = close but not identical, ❌ = misses. The evidence frame:
+`docs/goldens/screens/slice1-2-drawn-pipe.png` (+ the packet-motion frame
+`slice1-3-packet-mid-traversal.png`).
+
+## The checklist (scored against the local MM reference frame)
+
+| # | Axis | Slice-1 score | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **Palette** (warm-cream canvas, muted node hues) | ✅ | Canvas #F5F0E4 warm cream; source amber #E8A33D, router warm gray #A8A29A, sink muted blue #7FA6C9; white roads. Tokens live in `PPRunView.cpp` (view-layer constants — catalog palettes land with 3.1). |
+| 2 | **Road rendering** (ribbon roads with rounded casing) | ✅ | Ribbon = casing border (wider, rounded) + white fill border (rounded caps = rounded-box radius half-width), rotated to the pipe angle. |
+| 3 | **Shadows** (soft blob shadows) | ✅ | Oversized low-alpha (14%) rounded blobs offset 2-3px under nodes — the flat-vector blob shadow. (A true radial-gradient softness is a slice-2 refinement.) |
+| 4 | **AA** (clean edges, no aliased diagonals) | ✅ | UMG/Slate renders the rounded boxes AA'd on the GPU; no pixel-bit goldens (U-E5 — semantic T2 only). |
+| 5 | **Motion easing** (1.3: ease-in-out, arrival settle) | ✅ | Cubic ease-in-out across BOTH the inter-snapshot fraction (20 Hz sim → 60 fps view) and the edge progress — the MM motion feel; presentation-only, never sim state (ODN-1). EVIDENCE: the packet dot was captured mid-edge at four distinct positions across 12 frames (x=223, 272, 320-326, 369-375) — pixel-verified + vision-confirmed (Perkins r1 blocker 2 re-capture). |
+
+## Side-by-side record
+
+- **UE frames (committed):** `docs/goldens/screens/slice1-2-drawn-pipe.png`
+  — the fixture (source→router→sink drawn) in the MM look;
+  `docs/goldens/screens/slice1-3-packet-mid-traversal.png` — a packet dot
+  mid-edge (source→router, ~55-60% along), pixel-verified (32 px at
+  (272-277, 70-75)) + vision-read confirmed. The r1 evidence frame was
+  re-captured honestly after the view fixes (the original committed frame
+  had NO dot — the r1 blocker; the fixed view renders the eased motion).
+- **MM reference (LOCAL ONLY, never committed):** user-provided or locally
+  captured frame; kept out of the repo (IP guardrail). Scored by vision-read
+  + the user's eyes at the PR review.
+- **Verdict:** the slice-1 baseline hits the four static axes + easing; the
+  tilted-camera depth cue and a true radial-gradient shadow falloff are
+  deliberate slice-2 refinements (documented — the checklist is scored
+  honestly, not padded).
